<title>SINGAPORE: Fire at Mobil Singapore, maintenance unaffected.</title>
<headline>Fire at Mobil Singapore, maintenance unaffected.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-03-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>A fire at Mobil Oil Singapore's 280,000-barrel-per-day (bpd) refinery on March 25, has not disrupted its scheduled maintenance shutdown, a company spokeswoman said on Wednesay.</p>
<p>&quot;A very minor flash fire occurred at its refinery yesterday at about 2 pm. The fire was extinguished within 5 minutes with no disruptions to its turnaround activities,&quot; she said in a statement.  </p>
<p>Last month, a company spokesman said the Jurong plant on the west coast of Singapore will shut for about a month from March 15 for maintenance and debottlenecking to raise its capacity to 300,000-bpd.</p>
<p>-- Singapore Newsroom (+65-870-3086)</p>
</text>
